hweh, the God of Israel, under whose wings you have come to take refuge.”","source":"web"},{"ref":"2 Samuel 22:3","note":"God is my rock in whom I take refuge; my shield, and the horn of my salvation, my high tower, and my refuge. My savior, you save me from violence.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Psalm 2:12","note":"Give sincere homage to the Son, lest he be angry, and you perish on the way, for his wrath will soon be kindled. Blessed are all those who take refuge in him.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Proverbs 14:32","note":"The wicked is brought down in his calamity, but in death, the righteous has a refuge.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Isaiah 14:32","note":"What will they answer the messengers of the nation? That Yahweh has founded Zion, and in her the afflicted of his people will take refuge.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Nahum 1:7","note":"Yahweh is good, a stronghold in the day of trouble; and he knows those who take refuge in him.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}